The following code snippet contains a bug:

```php
    protected function storePhpBlocks($value)
    {
        return preg_replace_callback('/(?<!@)@php(.*?)@endphp/s', function ($matches) {
            return $this->storeRawBlock("<?php{$matches[1]}?>");
        }, $value);
    }
```

The code fails the following tests:

Test `Illuminate\Tests\View\Blade\BladePhpStatementsTest::testCompilationOfMixedPhpStatements`:
            
```php
    public function testCompilationOfMixedPhpStatements()
    {
        $string = '@php($set = true) @php ($hello = \'hi\') @php echo "Hello world" @endphp';
        $expected = '<?php ($set = true); ?> <?php ($hello = \'hi\'); ?> <?php echo "Hello world" ?>';
        $this->assertEquals($expected, $this->compiler->compileString($string));
    }
```

The error message is:

```
Failed asserting that two strings are equal.
```

Please provide a fixed version of the buggy function, and only that function without additional imports. Make sure the code is between ``` and ```.
